  <description
  >&lt;h2&gt;Date only: add one calendar month&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The picker returns a Salesforce Date. The Chrono Adjust action adds one month, constraining the day to the end of the target month.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Try the default &lt;b&gt;31 January 2026&lt;/b&gt;: the result should be &lt;b&gt;28 February 2026&lt;/b&gt;. No timezone is involved.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
  <formulas>
    <name>InitialValue</name>
    <dataType>Date</dataType>
    <expression>DATE(2026, 1, 31)</expression>
  </formulas>
